# arch-replay-vocabulary.cases — the case inputs both halves read, one CASE record per line.
#
# CASE|<case-id>|<mutation>|<replays>
#
# The frozen trace this corpus replays is arch-replay-vocabulary.ledger.jsonl: sixteen rows that
# exercise the durable event vocabulary end to end over one seeded swarm. `mutation` is what the
# replay applies to the frozen trace before folding it: `none` replays it as frozen,
# `forged_kind` replaces row 7 with a kind no vocabulary admits, `missing_field` strips the
# participant field from row 11's payload so the shape vocabulary cannot decode it, and
# `driver_row` replaces row 13 with a runtime-composed row the fold knows and the contract's
# caller set does not. `replays` is `once`, or `twice` to fold the same trace into two fresh maps
# and compare the projections byte for byte.
CASE|vocabulary-full|none|once
CASE|vocabulary-rerun|none|twice
CASE|vocabulary-forged-kind|forged_kind|once
CASE|vocabulary-missing-field|missing_field|once
CASE|vocabulary-driver-row|driver_row|once
